  "origin": "Shiva software by Todd Murphy (signal templates licensed from Persinger and Koren)",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's simple Shiva 'amygdala and hippocampus signals in sequence' session in its Fast (3×) version: the alternating amygdala and hippocampal bursts are played three times faster, stepped counter-clockwise around the head. Murphy states the pair 'should elicit a greater limbic activation than either of them alone'.",
  "setting": "Dark, quiet room, eyes closed, relaxed without meditating or falling asleep. Shiva offers 20, 30 and 60-min versions; start with the short one.",
  "schedule": "At most once a week, never on consecutive days; up to 6 sessions, then a 21-day break.",
  "notes": "Coils sit on Murphy's Shiva ring (Fp1, FT7, TP7, O1, O2, TP8, FT8, Fp2; one coil per site instead of Shiva's coil pairs) and fire one at a time counter-clockwise seen from above (back-to-front over the right side), 10, 12 … 20 ms per coil (Murphy's lecture example; Shiva's own step table is unpublished). Phase 1 (20 min) is the 20-min version; phase 2 makes it the 30-min version (a 60-min Shiva version also exists). The normal-speed stand-ins (amygdala: built-in accelerating burst, 230 points × 3 ms, 6 → 30 Hz; hippocampus: 4 theta bursts of 4 biphasic pulses at 3-ms points, bursts every 186 ms = the vendor's 5.4 Hz LTP peak; about 4 s of silence after each) are played here at 1-ms points, three times faster: a 0.23-s amygdala burst sweeping 18 → 90 Hz, 1.33 s of silence, a 0.25-s hippocampal train with bursts every 62 ms (16 Hz) and pulses 3 ms apart, 1.33 s of silence (cycle 3.1 s). Murphy's Shakti 'high-speed' signals likewise use 1-ms points and drop the latency; whether Shiva's fast version shortens or drops it is not published, so it is shortened 3× with the rest of the signal, as in the project's other Shiva fast sessions. Both signal files are proprietary, so these are approximations. Independent double-blind tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005; Gendle & McGrath 2012). Try the normal-speed version first; not for people with epilepsy; stop at once if distressed. Murphy reports headaches in about 2% of users of an earlier version of the technology, mostly with hippocampal signals, and advises lowering the intensity by a third.",
  "targets": ["left-amygdala", "right-amygdala", "left-hippocampus-head", "left-hippocampus-body", "left-hippocampus-tail", "right-hippocampus-head", "right-hippocampus-body", "right-hippocampus-tail"],
  "source": "Murphy, Shiva demo: Amygdala and hippocampus signals in sequence https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/shiva/shiva_demo/amygdala_hippocampus_page.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: What are 'Rapid' and 'High-Speed' signals? https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm ; Murphy, Mood enhancement / feelgood (8 Coil Shakti; two signals 'one after the other' with a four-second latency) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/rotating/shakti_happiness.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Random Theta Band output (LTP spectral peak 5.4 Hz) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/5jut4ranconsent.htm ; Murphy, Shiva demo: Consumer information https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/shiva/shiva_demo/shiva_infomed_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shiva demo: Magnetic coil locations https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/shiva/shiva_demo/locations.htm ; Murphy, Psychic Skills & Miracles lecture (coil steps of 10, 12 ... 20 ms) https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tmC1174POpA ; Murphy, Shiva demo: Session lengths https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/shiva/shiva_demo/session_length.htm ; Ryczko & Persinger 2002, Percept Mot Skills 95:592 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12434855/ ; Granqvist et al. 2005, Neurosci Lett 379:1 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15849873/ ; Gendle & McGrath 2012, Percept Mot Skills 114:217 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22582690/",
